{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.AdditiveResidualSimplex","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.AdditiveResidualSimplex","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.simplex_solve_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.simplex_solve_unique","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/AdditiveResidualSimplex.lean#L124-L134","doc":"**(S″) Uniqueness of the simplex coefficients** (unit-triangular system): two\ncoefficient triples with the same three residual values are equal.  With (S′)\nthis makes the decomposition a bijection — 0 free parameters, so `μ₂ = 0` is a\n*forced* structural fact, not a fitted one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.simplex_solve_exists","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.simplex_solve_exists","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/AdditiveResidualSimplex.lean#L113-L122","doc":"**(S′) The simplex decomposition is an exact 0-parameter solve.**  For any\nthree residual values `m₂, m₃, m₄` at A = 2, 3, 4 there is a *unique* triple\n`(μ₂, μ₃, μ₄)` reproducing them — the lower-triangular counts matrix\n`[[1,0,0],[3,1,0],[6,4,1]]` is unit-determinant.  Existence: the explicit\nback-substitution. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.residual_edge_coeff_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.residual_edge_coeff_zero","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/AdditiveResidualSimplex.lean#L104-L111","doc":"**(S) The 2-body/edge coefficient of the residual is exactly 0.**  Given the\nderived deuteron constraint `M(2) = 0`, the simplex decomposition forces the\n2-body coefficient `μ₂ = 0`, regardless of `μ₃, μ₄`.  So the residual has **no\nedge component**: it is a pure ≥3-body (triangle + tetrahedron) object. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.simplexA4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.simplexA4","kind":"def","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/AdditiveResidualSimplex.lean#L102-L102","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.simplexA3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.simplexA3","kind":"def","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/AdditiveResidualSimplex.lean#L101-L101","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.simplexA2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.simplexA2","kind":"def","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/AdditiveResidualSimplex.lean#L98-L100","doc":"The full simplex value `M(A) = μ₂·C(A,2) + μ₃·C(A,3) + μ₄·C(A,4)`, recorded at\nthe three rows A = 2, 3, 4 by their derived counts. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.deuteron_forces_edge_weight_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.deuteron_forces_edge_weight_zero","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/AdditiveResidualSimplex.lean#L88-L94","doc":"**(R′) The edge weight is forced to 0 by the deuteron.**  If a model instance\n*does* satisfy the derived deuteron constraint `modelA2 s t = 0`, then its edge\nweight `s` is `0`.  Consequently the frustration ratio κ = t/s has denominator\n`0` — it is structurally ill-posed on the derived data. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.model_refuted_at_deuteron","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.model_refuted_at_deuteron","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/AdditiveResidualSimplex.lean#L79-L86","doc":"**(R) The #4316 bond−frustration model is refuted at the deuteron.**  The\nderived third point is `M(2) = 0` (deuteron self-reference).  Any positively-\nscaled (`s > 0`) instance of the model predicts `M(2) = s > 0 ≠ 0`, so it cannot\nreproduce the deuteron.  Formally: no `s > 0` gives `modelA2 s t = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.modelA4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.modelA4","kind":"def","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/AdditiveResidualSimplex.lean#L77-L77","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.modelA3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.modelA3","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/AdditiveResidualSimplex.lean#L76-L76","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.modelA2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.modelA2","kind":"def","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/AdditiveResidualSimplex.lean#L70-L75","doc":"The bond−frustration model value at nucleon number `A`, in the #4316\nparametrisation `M(A) = s·C(A,2) − t·C(A,3)` (edge weight `s`, raw triangle\nweight `t = κ·s`).  We record the three relevant rows by their derived simplex\ncounts:\n`C(2,2)=1, C(2,3)=0`; `C(3,2)=3, C(3,3)=1`; `C(4,2)=6, C(4,3)=4`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}